Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-10, no third-party content: a
one-sheet schematic of two wires that touch nothing, the first from
(50.8, 76.2) to (50.8, 101.6) mm with the local label NET_A at its lower end,
the second from (76.2, 50.8) to (127, 50.8) mm with the local label NET_B at
its right end, and the project file. The first wire's upper end and the
second wire's left end are the same distance from the origin, (x, y) and
(y, x): engines before run 12's rebuild (kicad cc/main 8ea2dfa0) looked up
connection points through less<>, which compares lengths, joined the two ends
into one net and found NET_A and NET_B on it, which tests/e2e/check.spec.ts
refuses. The KiCad files carry no comment (their formats have none), so this
file holds their license.
